%I A401396 #10 Oct 31 2026 16:56:29
%S A401396 1,4,22,169,1819,41104,11679328
%N A401396 The number of semirings with one of size n up to isomorphism.
%C A401396 A semiring is a set S with two binary operations + and * such that (S, +) is a commutative semigroup, and (S, *) is a semigroup, and multiplication distributes over addition. A semiring with one requires (S, *) to have an identity 1, such that 1 * x = x * 1 = x for all x in S.
%H A401396 J. Edwards, J. D. Mitchell, and P. Ragavan, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.03709">Counting finite semirings</a>, arXiv:2507.03709 [math.RA], 2025-2026. See Table 1.
%F A401396 Since all semirings with one are semirings, a(n) <= A401124(n).
%Y A401396 Cf. A000001, A001423, A027623, A027851, A305858, A401124, A401395.
